{"id":22105,"title":"isocubes: Voxel Data Visualization with Isometric Cubes","url":"https://doi.org/10.32614/cran.package.isocubes","final_url":"https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/isocubes/isocubes.pdf","year":2025,"kind":"paper","source":"openalex","doi":"10.32614/cran.package.isocubes","arxiv":null,"sha256":"f56f1c350b69367601ea6cd9f98e53556498207a9036c656b095980a6cf1a196","ctype":"application/pdf","text_src":"oa","fetched_at":1793059150.1521287,"text_chars":17989,"abstract":"A voxel is a representation of a value on a regular, three-dimensional grid; it is the 3D equivalent of a 2D pixel. Voxel data can be visualised with this package using fixed viewpoint isometric cubes for each data point. This package also provides sample voxel data and tools for transforming the data.","file":null,"marks":["unofficial"],"links":["https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/isocubes/isocubes.pdf","https://doi.org/10.32614/cran.package.isocubes"],"cited_by":[{"path":"2279-rotation-transformation.md","name":"Rotation Transformation","k":2},{"path":"4046-voxel-visibility-map-computation.md","name":"Voxel Visibility Map Computation","k":1},{"path":"6766-coordinate-conversion-utilities.md","name":"Coordinate Conversion Utilities","k":5},{"path":"11001-voxel-mesh-generation-cube-construction.md","name":"Voxel Mesh Generation (Cube Construction)","k":4},{"path":"8499-specific-implicit-primitives.md","name":"Specific Implicit Primitives","k":3},{"path":"2873-translation-matrix-construction.md","name":"Translation Matrix Construction","k":2},{"path":"14251-coordinate-alignment.md","name":"Coordinate Alignment","k":1},{"path":"14250-implicit-function-evaluation.md","name":"Implicit Function Evaluation","k":1}]}